.TH LIUXIN-INGEST 1 "2026-10-23" "LiuXin-alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liuxin-ingest \- select a local or remote acquisition workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liuxin ingest
.I SOURCE
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin ingest web
.RI [ URL ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin ingest disk
.I PATH
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin ingest
.I subcommand
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
The ingest family exposes several source workflows.
Choose the workflow according to where the source exists and whether remote
files should merely be registered or also downloaded.
.TP
.B web URL
Walk a bounded HTTP(S) source and record remote candidates by default.
.B \-\-download
acquires verified copies into managed storage;
.B \-\-registered-only
selects previously recorded candidates without re-crawling navigation pages.
Use
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1)
for filters, budgets, saved runs and complete examples.
.TP
.B SOURCE
The concise local-host mixed-file workflow, equivalent to the detailed
.B liuxin storage ingest
operator. On Linux the positional source form detects directories,
SquashFS/ext4 images and block devices and requires a verified read-only mount.
Use
.B liuxin storage ingest \-\-help
for its source-protection, discovery, preflight and budget controls.
.TP
.B disk PATH
Submit local-disk ingestion as a managed job on the Core host.
The path must be visible to Core; a remote client does not upload it implicitly.
.TP
.B remote-html
Retain the older native/wget HTML registration workflow for legacy files and
Store declarations. It does not acquire payloads.
New remote-registration and download workflows should use
.BR web .
.TP
.B runs list|show|watch|issues|resume
Inspect and resume the CLI-local mixed-file workflow's reports.
Web runs instead use
.BR "web URL \-\-list" ,
.B web \-\-status RUN_UUID
and
.BR "web \-\-resume RUN_UUID" .
.TP
.B formats
Report available ingest format information.
.SH LOCAL LIVE STATUS
Interactive local imports display a Rich panel on stderr with attempt counters,
current activity, elapsed time, memory, cache bytes and free-space headroom.
Nested discovery has no known overall total, so no percentage or ETA is shown.
JSON receipts remain on stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-progress " auto|rich|plain"
Select the import or watcher display. Auto uses Rich on an interactive stderr
and plain output when redirected. Rich explicitly forces terminal rendering.
.TP
.B \-\-no-console-progress
Suppress the import display, including an explicit Rich selection.
.PP
Attach from another terminal using
.B liuxin ingest runs watch RUN_UUID
with
.BR "\-\-system-root ROOT" ,
.BR "\-\-profile PROFILE" ,
or
.BR "\-\-log-directory DIRECTORY" .
The watcher selects the newest attempt once and exits on its terminal event.
It reads local logs only. Ctrl-C detaches the watcher without signalling the
import; Ctrl-C in the import terminal requests a cooperative stop.
Attach again after resuming to select the new attempt.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Watch option: display one snapshot and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh-seconds " SECONDS"
Watch redraw interval; default 1, minimum 0.1. Resource observations still follow
the import's resource-interval-seconds setting (default 5 seconds).
.PP
Sample age is displayed. Silence beyond the greater of 15 seconds or three
resource intervals is marked stale, with liveness unknown. A killed importer
without a terminal event leaves the watcher waiting until detached.
Reads and partial-line buffers are bounded; large logs start at recent telemetry.
Older logs may show unknown metrics. Watching does not supervise or daemonize
the importer, and requires read access to its logs on the original CLI host.
.SH LOCAL RESOURCE PROTECTION
Local mixed ingest enforces a free-space reserve before catalogue startup and
at safe boundaries during the run. It checks the catalogue, cache, temporary,
log, report and lock filesystems, plus the WSL backing drive when applicable.
.TP
.BI \-\-min-free-mib " N"
Positive reserve on each output volume; default 2048 MiB.
Known member spools and nested-container copies require additional headroom.
.TP
.BI \-\-resource-interval-seconds " SECONDS"
Independent resource sampling interval; default 5, minimum 0.1.
JSONL resource samples include capacity, Linux memory counters, current
source/archive/member and per-attempt cache reservation/materialization bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-host-space-path " PATH"
Repeatable existing host-drive directory. Explicit paths override automatic WSL
backing-drive discovery. Use the volume containing the distribution's virtual
disk; it is not necessarily C:. Unavailable host detection requires this option.
.PP
The default log level is INFO, retaining aggregate checkpoints and resource
samples. DEBUG adds per-object audit records. The human log rotates; JSONL
remains append-only and its volume is protected by the free-space reserve.
.PP
A resource stop returns exit 1 and status resource_stopped. Release space and
use liuxin ingest runs resume RUN_UUID with the original system selector and
mount privileges. Completed records deduplicate. These are cooperative checks,
not disk reservations: running backend operations and unrelated writers can
consume space before the next boundary. No automatic cache or log deletion occurs.
.SH CONNECTIONS
Use
.BR \-\-system-root " " DIRECTORY
or another connection selector from
.BR liuxin (1).
Web requests and managed-job staging occur on the Core host.
Web ingest needs no root privileges. Local Linux source mounting may require
privileges; use an explicit system selector when invoking it through
.BR sudo (8).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-download \-\-registered-only \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web \-\-status RUN_UUID \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin storage ingest \-\-help
liuxin ingest runs watch RUN_UUID \e
  \-\-system-root /srv/liuxin
liuxin ingest runs watch RUN_UUID \e
  \-\-log-directory /srv/liuxin/logs \-\-once \-\-progress plain
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR liuxin (1),
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1)
